Track 3: The Gardener’s Last Calibration
- Story & Context: Years after the lab was abandoned, the local townsfolk told stories of the "Ghost of the Canopy" who kept the lights blinking in the ruins. They found the main server room overgrown with vines that pulsed with a steady, electric green rhythm, echoing the final, unfinished symphony Elias had composed. "We bloom in the current, forever out of reach," the brass melody seemed to declare, echoing through the empty, leaf-choked hallways.
